{"type":"message","id":"2aaddd32","parentId":"4189f4d7","timestamp":"2026-04-02T07:10:12.758Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see there's already a `scnet` provider that has DeepSeek-V3.2 configured for free. Let me check if there's already a DeepSeek provider configured. Looking at the config, I see:\n\n1. There's already a `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` in env: `sk-4937ba36104841a8be0cb2b82c703c28`\n2. There's a `scnet` provider with `DeepSeek-V3.2` model which is free (cost: 0)\n\nBut the user wants to use their own API key `sk-7efc0cb52584445399ba99eb17df91b8`.\n\nLooking at the config structure, to add DeepSeek properly I need to:\n1. Add the API key to env\n2. Add a deepseek provider in models.providers\n\nBut actually, looking more carefully - the user just sent their API key. I should probably use the config set command properly. Let me try using the env section to set the DeepSeek API key.\n\nActually, the config file shows `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` already exists in env. Let me try to update it.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The skill says to use:\n```\nopenclaw config set model deepseek-chat\nopenclaw config set api_key sk-xxx\n```\n\nBut that didn't work. Let me try setting it in the env section instead.","thinkingSignature":"b8a9163ce061079ddbe5a98e9e76a65ee8b21dc52c45319e7ff1836612004401"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_su16v861ce0c_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config set env.DEEPSEEK_API_KEY sk-7efc0cb52584445399ba99eb17df91b8"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":6020,"output":341,"cacheRead":12004,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18365,"cost":{"input":0.0018059999999999999,"output":0.00040919999999999997,"cacheRead":0.0007202399999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029354399999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775113798978,"responseId":"061d4947a3981c4be78a8a57535341a6"}}
