{"type":"message","id":"565ceb9b","parentId":"9677ac68","timestamp":"2026-04-02T07:10:31.029Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the DeepSeek API key has been updated. But I notice the config already has a `scnet` provider with a free DeepSeek-V3.2 model. Let me also check if we need to add a dedicated DeepSeek provider for the user's API key.\n\nActually, looking at the existing config, there's already a `scnet` provider that has `DeepSeek-V3.2` with free pricing. The user's new API key should work with that.\n\nBut to properly use DeepSeek with the user's API key, I should probably add a DeepSeek provider configuration. Let me check if the config needs a DeepSeek provider.\n\nActually, the user's API key is now set. Let me also check if we need to add the deepseek provider. Looking at the models section, there's no \"deepseek\" provider - only \"scnet\" which has DeepSeek-V3.2.\n\nLet me add a deepseek provider so the user can use `deepseek-chat` as the model. I'll need to add the provider configuration.\n\nActually, the easier approach might be to just use the existing scnet provider's DeepSeek-V3.2 which is free. But the user specifically wanted to configure DeepSeek with their API key, probably to get better rate limits or use DeepSeek's official API.\n\nLet me add a deepseek provider to the config properly.","thinkingSignature":"8f00db6fe263132c68e68330134e74ddab2b69d323400a47191f140320bb7c6d"},{"type":"text","text":"API Key 已更新。不过臣注意到配置中还没有 DeepSeek 的专用provider，让臣帮主公加上：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1lwf1qdzbixg_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config set models.providers.deepseek --provider-source api_key --provider-base-url https://api.deepseek.com --provider-api openai-completions"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":6492,"output":355,"cacheRead":12004,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18851,"cost":{"input":0.0019475999999999999,"outp